      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778536596709,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Exercise 3.13: Consider the following make-cycle procedure, which uses the last-pair\nprocedure defined in Exercise 3.12:\n\n(define (make-cycle x)\n    (set-cdr! (last-pair x) x)\n    x)\n\nDraw a box-and-pointer diagram that shows the structure z created by:\n\n(define z (make-cycle (list 'a 'b 'c)))\n\nWhat happens if we try to compute (last-pair z)? Answer: infinite loop",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Exercise 3.13: Consider the following make-cycle procedure, which uses the last-pair\nprocedure defined in Exercise 3.12:\n\n(define (make-cycle x)\n    (set-cdr! (last-pair x) x)\n    x)\n\nDraw a box-and-pointer diagram that shows the structure z created by:\n\n(define z (make-cycle (list 'a 'b 'c)))\n\nWhat happens if we try to compute (last-pair z)? Answer: infinite loop",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
